<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     10. FAQ — clean accordion
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="s-faq">
  <div class="s-section-head reveal-up">
    <span class="s-badge">FAQ</span>
    <h2 class="s-h2">Questions we get every week.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="s-faq-list reveal-up">

    <div class="s-faq-item">
      <button class="s-faq-q" aria-expanded="false">What's the difference between SEO and AEO?<span class="s-chevron"></span></button>
      <div class="s-faq-a"><strong>SEO gets you ranked in Google; AEO gets your content cited by AI models like ChatGPT, Claude, and Gemini.</strong> The two overlap but require different content structure. AEO demands direct-answer blocks, entity markup, and fact density that traditional SEO content often lacks. We build both simultaneously.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="s-faq-item">
      <button class="s-faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Do you specialise in Web3 and crypto?<span class="s-chevron"></span></button>
      <div class="s-faq-a"><strong>Yes — Web3, crypto, DeFi, and fintech are our primary verticals.</strong> These niches have specific keyword dynamics and require writers who understand the technical content. We've ranked clients for terms like "crypto exchange platform" and "DeFi wallet development" in markets where Google's ad restrictions make organic visibility especially valuable.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="s-faq-item">
      <button class="s-faq-q" aria-expanded="false">How do you get my brand cited by ChatGPT and Claude?<span class="s-chevron"></span></button>
      <div class="s-faq-a"><strong>AI models cite sources that are authoritative, factually dense, clearly structured, and well-referenced across the web.</strong> We build pages with direct-answer blocks, specific numbers, named-entity co-occurrence, and structured data — then back that content with editorial links from publications AI models are known to pull from.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="s-faq-item">
      <button class="s-faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Do you guarantee specific rankings?<span class="s-chevron"></span></button>
      <div class="s-faq-a"><strong>No agency can guarantee specific positions — anyone who does is either lying or selling manipulative tactics that risk a Google penalty.</strong> What we guarantee is a rigorous process: technical fixes, intent-matched content, and editorially earned links. Our client results speak for what that produces.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="s-faq-item">
      <button class="s-faq-q" aria-expanded="false">What does reporting look like?<span class="s-chevron"></span></button>
      <div class="s-faq-a"><strong>We report through a live Ahrefs dashboard plus Google Search Console data and a monthly written summary.</strong> You see keyword positions, traffic trends, new backlinks acquired, and domain authority movement. Direct access to the source tools — no custom portal hiding the data.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="s-faq-item">
      <button class="s-faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Do you handle international SEO?<span class="s-chevron"></span></button>
      <div class="s-faq-a"><strong>Yes — we've run campaigns across 50+ markets including complex hreflang structures for Arabic, Mandarin, Korean, and European languages.</strong> We also handle local SEO for clients in Dubai (VARA), Singapore (MAS), and UK (FCA) markets where regulatory entity mentions drive significant organic traffic.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="s-faq-item">
      <button class="s-faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can you work alongside our existing content team?<span class="s-chevron"></span></button>
      <div class="s-faq-a"><strong>Yes — we work as an extension of in-house teams.</strong> We can handle strategy while your team executes, or produce content directly for review. We document everything — keyword maps, briefs, internal linking plans — so your team has full visibility.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="s-faq-item">
      <button class="s-faq-q" aria-expanded="false">What tools do you use?<span class="s-chevron"></span></button>
      <div class="s-faq-a"><strong>Ahrefs, Semrush, Screaming Frog, Google Search Console, Surfer SEO, Clearscope, PageSpeed Insights, and the Perplexity API for AEO validation.</strong> For AI citation testing we run prompts across ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, and Perplexity against your target queries and track mention share over time.</div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

